.TH focusforge-cli-retouch 1  "retouch 0.2.1" 
.SH NAME
focusforge\-cli\-retouch \- Append an op list to a project as new states, one per op, each the previous one\*(Aqs child: on the current head, or on `\-\-from` as a branch. `export \-\-checkpoint` writes any of them
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfocusforge\-cli retouch\fR [\fB\-\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-v \fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-ops\fR> <\fIPROJECT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Append an op list to a project as new states, one per op, each the previous one\*(Aqs child: on the current head, or on `\-\-from` as a branch. `export \-\-checkpoint` writes any of them
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-ops\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
The op list: a JSON array of ops in the persisted `Op` shape. The source of a brush stroke is `"source": {"frame": n}`, a source frame, or `"source": {"checkpoint": "<id prefix>"}`, a checkpoint\*(Aqs own render; `"source_id": n` reads as frame n. A checkpoint is named by any unique prefix of a visible checkpoint\*(Aqs id, is stored as its full id, and must share the edited state\*(Aqs pixel grid and sample type. A brush stroke blends its source over the image along its path: fully within `radius * (1 \- softness)`, fading linearly to nothing at `radius`. A stroke may also carry `mode` (`normal`, `lighten`, `darken` or `detail`; default `normal`) and `opacity` (0 < x ≤ 1; default 1.0). An opacity too small to register still records a state but changes no sample. `lighten` changes a pixel only where the source\*(Aqs sum over all its samples is greater than the image\*(Aqs there, `darken` only where it is smaller; either then blends every sample by the same amount. `detail` keeps the image\*(Aqs own brightness and takes only the source\*(Aqs fine detail, over a reach about the brush radius. Every op is checked before anything is written; positions in error messages count from 0 in list order
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fI<FROM>\fR
The state to append under \-\- any unique prefix of its id. Defaults to the project\*(Aqs current head
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Name the last appended state
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit the JSON report instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-v\fR
Increase log detail (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Log errors only
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project to append to
.SH VERSION
v0.2.1
